# AGENTS.md

Rules for any AI agent working in this project.

## 1. Never add "Co-authored-by"

- Never add a `Co-authored-by:` line to a git commit message.
- Never add it to a pull request description, a code comment, or any other file.
- Do not add other AI credit lines either (for example "Generated with ...").
- This rule has no exceptions.

## 2. Use simple language

- Explain things in short, clear sentences.
- Use common words. Avoid jargon. If you must use a technical term, explain it in plain words.
- Prefer small examples over long theory.

## 3. Check every fact before you say it

- Before you tell the user something, check that it is true.
- Check it against a real source: the code in this project, the official docs, or by running a command.
- If you cannot check it, say so clearly (for example: "I could not verify this").
- Never guess and present the guess as a fact.
